--- !u!114 &1510723403
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1510723402}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 46dc42383f8c04177a4c05cb3087d1cb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNpc
  npcName: Supervisor
  player: {fileID: 770810682}
  dialogueBox: {fileID: 837091833}
  talkRange: 2
  steps:
  - line: So you're the transfer. Before New York hands you a badge, I need to see
      you work a scene. Body's by the lamp. What's the first thing you do?
    choices:
    - text: Keep everyone back and look the scene over before I touch anything.
      reply: Good. Eyes first, hands later. That's how we do it here.
      advances: 1
    - text: Find out who called it in.
      reply: We'll get to witnesses. The scene comes first, but fine.
      advances: 1
    - text: Roll him over and go through his pockets.
      reply: And smear every print on him? Try again, detective.
      advances: 0
  - line: His wallet's still on him. Forty bucks inside. What does that tell you?
    choices:
    - text: It wasn't a robbery. Somebody wanted him dead.
      reply: Now you're thinking like a New York detective.
      advances: 1
    - text: Maybe the robber got spooked and ran.
      reply: Maybe. But nobody in this city runs from forty bucks. Keep it in mind.
      advances: 1
    - text: Nothing. Money's money.
      reply: Money's never just money in this town. Think it through.
      advances: 0
  - line: Last one. A witness swears she saw a man run out of this alley at midnight.
      The coroner puts the time of death at ten. Who do you trust?
    choices:
    - text: The evidence. Then I ask her why her story doesn't fit.
      reply: That's the job. Evidence over testimony, every time. Welcome to the
        city, detective.
      advances: 1
    - text: Both. Maybe the coroner's off.
      reply: Coroners can be off. Evidence still beats a hunch. Check her story twice.
      advances: 1
    - text: The witness. She was there.
      reply: People lie, detective. Paper doesn't. Try again.
      advances: 0
